for this project you will need the  printed copy of the template scissors  and tape cut out the five strips on the  dotted line  make sure to separate the co-joined  strips the green orange and yellow tabs  have to remain attached to their  respective strips proteins are polymer  chains of amino acid residues each  number on the model represents one amino  acid residue insulin has two chains tina  is green chain v is blue tape together  the two pieces of the a chain green so  that residue lemon is back to back in  the two pieces tape together the three  blue pieces of the B chain by  overlapping the gray tabs at the ends so  that all the numbers are visible on one  side and all the numbers are in order  some sections of amino acid chains curl  and formed alpha helixes due to hydrogen  bonds between NH and co groups the helix  regions on the model are marked on the  chains with darker shades of green and  blue start with residues 1 and 5 and  form of hydrogen bond between co and NH  and taped together keep creating the  hydrogen bonds until you reach the end  of the darker colored area when you  reach residue 6 make sure the green cap  is on the outside of the helix create  another alpha helix starting with  residues 17 and 21 keep creating  hydrogen bonds until you reach the end  of the darker colored area  starting with residues 7 and 11 form a  hydrogen bond keep creating the Alpha  helix until you reach the end of the  darker colored area  some amino acids give a turn to the  chain the turns are marked on chain B of  the paper model with the white dashed  lines fold outwards on the white dashed  lines to create the turn you can secure  the fold with tape  also note that chain B offs includes a  beta strand marked with a blue arrow the  structure of insulin is stabilized by  three disulfide bridges a disulfide  bridge --it is formed when a sulfur atom  from the residue cysteine forms a single  covalent bond with a sulfur atom from a  second cysteine the first disulfide  bridge connects two cysteines in a chain  a to form the bridge connect the green  tabs connect the yellow tabs matching  their shape while making sure the  colored size are facing the same way  connect the orange tabs matching their  shape while making sure that colored  sides are facing the same way  congratulations if you have completed  all the steps and your project looks  like the one shown here then you now  have your own insulin model
 

